.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-REPLAY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-replay - Deliberately replay one retained HTTP request to the same origin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel replay <tunnel> <capture-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Send one captured HTTP request again to the same tunnel origin. This repeats whatever the
request did, including side effects such as payments or writes. Name the capture by its ID
(from pb tunnel inspect) and pass --route when the tunnel has several routes. An idempotency
key is generated unless you pass --idempotency-key; reuse one key to retry safely.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for replay

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	explicit idempotency key for safe retry (generated when omitted)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--route\fP=""
	replay a capture from one route ID (required when the tunnel has several routes)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel replay web cap_123
  pb tunnel replay web cap_123 --route route_xyz --idempotency-key order-42
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
